I suppose it's the missing SUID/SGID flags on the executable.

In my environment /usr/bin/nethack is a link to a script
/usr/bin/nethack.tty and that script accesses the executable
nethack in the playground /usr/games/lib/nethackdir where
ls -l shows both 's' bits set...

-rwsr-sr-x    1 games    games     1787335 2003-12-08 00:48 nethack

Use chmod (as root) to set the flags accordingly.

